Z||000003||Spektyr||04-19-2001||04:37 PM||||"A shop"?<P>Donut shop?<P>Speed shop?<P>Lube shop?<P>I've been using Shamrock down on south Broadway for most of my Lincoln repairs (for those rare instances when it isn't running perfectly) but I haven't really found a shop I like 100% for those jobs I just don't feel like doing myself.  (10 below outside and you need to change the plugs.)<P>Okay, so I'm spoiled.<P>Anyway, I've walked into the local AutoZones, O'Reilly's, etc with strange questions often enough and gotten blank stares, stupid answers, and just plain wrong advice enough times that I've pretty much given up on them knowing anything about the parts I need to do the work on my car.  So if you know of a place that hires good people (above room-temperature IQ), I'd appreciate the heads up.<P>Those parts stores computers are great devices... if your car is still stock.<P>But then I've got a trunk-full of tools.  Stock is just the word for the parts I haven't replaced yet.<P>Oh, and if you know a place that won't laugh at me if I ask for a fat anti-sway bar for my 1989 Lincoln Town Car, let me know.  The guys at AutoZone looked at me like they were going to call the men in white coats.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spektyr||04-19-2001||10:06 PM||||Woo Hoo!<P>Stock V6 4speed... white, I'm guessing 1985 GT (the driver's side door sticker is ruined, just in the year location).  I'll find out for sure when I get the title.<P>Damn if it ain't pretty quick stock!  (can't wait to start modifying)<P>I'm ready to cruise, just let me know when.||||reg||1
Z||000005||cmc||04-19-2001||11:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektyr:<BR><B>Woo Hoo!<P>Stock V6 4speed... white, I'm guessing 1985 GT (the driver's side door sticker is ruined, just in the year location).  I'll find out for sure when I get the title.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What's the 10th digit in the VIN?  That will tell you the year.  For example, if it's J, it's an '88.  If it's H, it's '87, if it's G, it's '86, and if it's F, it's an '85.  (I think you get the picture...).  They don't use the letter "I" because it can be confused quite easily with the number 1.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tweek||04-20-2001||12:08 AM||||Write down the VIN, and go to <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net/vin.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.net/vin.html</A>  and put it in and it will tell you what kind of car you have.<P>If you post the VIN here I will run it through carfax for ya too..<P>Another way to tell is if it really is an '85 then look at the front and rear facias. If they have the black bumper pads then it's not a GT, if it has the Aero moldings, then it is.||||reg||1
